# Phase 18 Producer runtime-settings gap audit and benchmark capture — 2026-10-13

- Starting revision: `0a3d949c` on `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate`. No code changes were made in this session.
- Audited the pinned RocketMQ 5.5.1 `DefaultMQProducer` and `DefaultMQProducerImpl` source at commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.
- Confirmed local P18-V01 Producer gaps: runtime async backpressure capacity changes currently have only pre-construction `ProducerConfig` setters; toggling async backpressure after construction is unavailable; retry response codes cannot be changed on an active Producer, while Java exposes a live mutable set. Java's public permit-adjust/lock helpers, `getCompressor`, and `initProduceAccumulator` also need explicit source-backed raw API dispositions.
- Captured `cargo bench -p rocketmq-classic --bench offline --locked` on macOS AArch64 / Apple M5 Max / Rust 1.85.0. Results: frame encode/decode 1,468.0 ns/op; Zstd record decode 1,098.5 ns/op; Producer request construction 929.2 ns/op; route lookup 14.3 ns/op; local TCP pending completion 65,799.4 ns/op. Allocation counts/bytes matched earlier runs. These are local observations, not thresholds.
- Updated the Phase 6 audit, Phase 7 Producer matrix, Phase 18 release checklist, and benchmark baseline. `git diff --check` passed. No tests were rerun because this session's changes are documentation-only; the current code revision's test and Clippy results remain those recorded in the preceding Phase 18 log.
- Still open beyond later manual validation: complete P18-V01 source/input/branch and Java reverse-export reconciliation; implement or explicitly resolve the Producer runtime-settings gaps; obtain current GitHub Ubuntu CI evidence; confirm the `0.1.0` release version and registry dependency resolution. Phase 19 Broker/Docker scenarios and any owner-only external checks remain future validation work.
